// tests/counter_contract.inc: the counter contract. Counters are ABI: one table,
// identical on every platform and in every build (ROCKETNET_DEV on or off), the
// union of every transport's rows, never behind a preprocessor condition. An id
// is never renumbered, renamed, removed or reused; a new counter is appended to
// sdk/rocketnet_counters.h and to this list in the same commit.
//
// One row per counter, in id order: ROCKETNET_COUNTER_CONTRACT( id, NAME, CLASS ).
// tools/check_counter_contract.py (lint) holds sdk/rocketnet_counters.h to this
// list; tests/test_unit_counter_contract.cpp reads the built table against it on
// every platform and in every build.
//
// A RELEASED line freezes the first <count> rows as a release shipped them:
// sha256 over "<id>\t<NAME>\t<CLASS>\n" for ids 0 .. count-1. The checker
// recomputes it, so a released row cannot change even when the header and this
// list change together. The release adds its line (docs/RELEASING.md).
//
// Rows alias by design: the shared rows (PREFILTER_TOO_SHORT and _TOO_LARGE,
// RECEIVE_DROPPED_FULL 224, RECEIVE_FAILED 225, SEND_FAILED, SEND_RING_FULL)
// and the transport rows 226-276 that say where (GSO_RECEIVE_DROPPED_SIZE,
// _OVERFLOW, _SOURCE, GSO_SEND_DROPPED and their URING_, IOCP_ and RIO_
// counterparts) count the same events, so a sum over every refusal row is not
// a count of distinct drops. standard/TRANSPORT.md t18 lists each alias.
//
